    "narrative": "For our September 26th slate, the lineup is anchored by **Vinnie Pasquantino** (75.15) and **James Wood** (73.49). **Vinnie Pasquantino** draws a highly favorable matchup against Bibee, where a 12% boost from the SP skill profile and a strong dynamic platoon edge make him our highest-rated producer. Meanwhile, **James Wood** is set to maximize his 10% leadoff boost and elite 0.404 xwOBA against Tong, making him our primary engine for Runs. **Corbin Carroll** (71.68) remains a high-floor start despite a slight drag from his elite-catcher-hold efficiency metric, as his upside in SB\u2014our scarcest category\u2014remains too vital to fade against Buehler. We are also monitoring **Josh Naylor**, who sits at a strong 72.51, benefiting significantly from the soft matchup against Ryan Johnson.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Austin Riley** (54.29). While his power profile is formidable, he fell just short of our target efficiency threshold against the tough arm of Ralston; the optimizer preferred the superior situational matchups of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Brice Turang**, both of whom are projected to deliver more consistent production in this specific Roto context. Note that **Moises Ballesteros**, **Cole Young**, and **Isaac Paredes** are all carrying \"Lineup Pending\" tags; while we have baked in historical placement for these projections, any shift down the order could necessitate a re-evaluation of their 40\u201365 range scores. **Griffin Conine** remains comfortably on the bench as his sub-40 score against Suter reflects the risks of a L/L platoon disadvantage, and we continue to steer clear of the injured **Tyler Soderstrom**.",
